# CMM Routers — local bearer tokens only.
# Host is fixed to 127.0.0.1 by schema; port lives in config/shared.json.
# Copy nothing secret into git: this file holds only the token variable names.
#
# CMM_ROUTER_TOKEN authenticates the CHAT profile (CMMChat). CHAT has no
# default tool access; it may use only Router-registered scoped actions that are
# explicitly granted server-side. This token can never authenticate AGENT.
CMM_ROUTER_TOKEN=
#
# CMM_CODE_ROUTER_TOKEN is the canonical AGENT profile bearer. AGENT is the
# harness/agent profile: Qoder, Hermes, Codex CLI and generic agents all
# authenticate the SAME profile, and tool calls are always executed by the
# client, never by the Router. AGENT may use tools only on providers whose
# structured upstream round-trip is proven (CHAT_AND_TOOLS); provider capability
# alone never grants tools to a client.
CMM_CODE_ROUTER_TOKEN=
#
# CMM_QODER_TOKEN is the legacy Qoder alias for the SAME AGENT profile. It is
# retained so installed setups keep working without migration; it is not a
# distinct role. When neither AGENT token is set there is no AGENT consumer.
CMM_QODER_TOKEN=
#
# Cavoti is an explicit PAYG route. It remains disabled in shared config and
# also requires a separate machine-local spend acknowledgement before the
# Router will register it. This example intentionally contains no secret value.
CAVOTI_API_KEY=
